{/*
  Boboddy docs is dark-only. Starlight's default ThemeProvider reads a
  stored preference or the `prefers-color-scheme` media query and can
  resolve to `data-theme="light"`. We replace it with a version that
  always pins `data-theme="dark"`, so there is no light-mode flash and no
  dependency on system/browser preference. `updatePickers` is kept as a
  no-op so nothing throws if any Starlight internals still call it (the
  `ThemeSelect` override renders no picker, so it never will in practice).

  This must stay inlined (`is:inline`) and run in `<head>`, matching the
  default implementation, so the theme is set before first paint.
*/}
<script is:inline>
	window.StarlightThemeProvider = {
		updatePickers() {},
	};
	document.documentElement.dataset.theme = "dark";
</script>
